b5Uw8xOUz4i1Al_Ql5lle7gaTc_sd-_snCTPf7CiPpMXr3ZxsDGhm_Ea43Fvmw1DoKni4M1xmGVqST8mv8UQjcwOHYe6gblwPs1vJrTDt4vdf5ppCcMbYPOAKRONsBr9J27Ohrk3iN3MCDYl7OISulJsgWeebmDqffV-dTdWmaE1_QORO7RhfHImVCMf3CW72PWvXHSO9-NYKrcn_yom_ndt5xbRo4rXr-D1zZZm3lUzu_8dRID1ohv6J4mWGdJjNV2ybJnQtWHkN3TvAN0nSihkNJR6QhUdsBCAFUiTGvbLQD_Frx-H_9dDWqCNphk7iM8WS6jHHVgjmS2n0XCiqzqUrROprlGe92BOBkH8Jn3mJEC9MMgL8UYeeu0KUXQs7shsW3qk-REn2vJU-rCEFCUIr_ftZ0GVi_Fllo92F-lU3A_XSbAdFloUXWtAYGggFA3wDsXDkqvL-i2ak928T0NOEvAgHfQQqQJZzGQAS8PJkY59BaIx-2pW-EfQD6ysWxrggEqXiir2kt9YXC-D8wAf2knyjAHqE3eqfYVwL4z1QClPsltdYKX8-87SXl3hD4BZgr4p0HiDPgmFbOkjGRpG5FeoY8u8RLcZskuqHpj4HuB8XGDMdVsZ0jClAZvArVVlMEaHYk33--RU7QhI93JgfRO4lbHLrzLs6AJIXbZu7i0SqHtYa3sWMCV_GwirfWKwVFuaDxvB1emVnkwtM3D63ciiZ5THmwGu5BR0B2SR-uS0Ptncq2Z3YPYJnqdAzbELN-OSgOVlaawIT4cnXCSVdDRk6djgunZ50xorV-iRJXCiCRU8pZxYP_u5D5bVgfsz7AnTMZEkmtp4EhFPFvaMxlXfcS91JhBDHpz3rvKrg5xIPYHnFL0DawdTyAWSjvGfIkkK_2XIGblgAPG1UGZb9gqe7TkPwverDkNT41IpFBSDxsobiksztAKlJx0z-u1zi-A2fPrnYNbCQEDzGBAWqp6zK-KdE21aTkDVcEv5beLz14vSSOPSa9wZUKYVvHVSn2XvoseK3t5ecNnwAa4Hvm7MIFKyOq-6OxCVRrgsgeyzFXK0BzicCvl8zsEHAXPdIS_M7xMIIHag29mY7NGTcOtcRuBuO8n2fgoU08dVQP8aXPDTe712GM2sgXrgsc="},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_05ead64b871aca2a016adb614597b08191824d80a3b9df6d77","call_id":"call_b138d1d5898440ec90ef87e7c2db58c5","name":"submit_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"header\":\"import Mathlib\\nopen scoped TensorProduct\\nnoncomputable def dividedPower (V : Type*) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] (f : V →ₗ[ℂ] V) (r : ℕ) : V →ₗ[ℂ] V := ((Nat.factorial r : ℂ)⁻¹) • (f ^ r)\\ndef LieIrreducible (K : Type*) [Field K] (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E] [Module K E] (x y h : E →ₗ[K] E) : Prop := Nontrivial E ∧ ∀ W : Submodule K E, (∀ z ∈ W, x z ∈ W) → (∀ z ∈ W, y z ∈ W) → (∀ z ∈ W, h z ∈ W) → W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤\\nstructure LatticeInput (lam : ℤ) (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] where\\n  V : Type*\\n  [vAdd : AddCommGroup V]\\n  [vMod : Module ℂ V]\\n  basisV : Module.Basis (Fin (lam.toNat + 1)) ℂ V\\n  basisM : Module.Basis (Fin (lam.toNat + 1)) ℤ M\\n  embed : M →ₗ[ℤ] V\\n  x : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  y : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  h : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  xM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  yM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  hM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  v : V\\n  basis_compatible : ∀ i, basisV i = embed (basisM i)\\n  embed_injective : Function.Injective embed\\n  complex_irreducible : LieIrreducible ℂ V x y h\\n  x_compatible : ∀ m, embed (xM m) = x (embed m)\\n  y_compatible : ∀ m, embed (yM m) = y (embed m)\\n  h_compatible : ∀ m, embed (hM m) = h (embed m)\\n  divided_x_preserves : ∀ r m, ∃ m', embed m' = dividedPower V x r (embed m)\\n  divided_y_preserves : ∀ r m, ∃ m', embed m' = dividedPower V y r (embed m)\\ndef LatticeInput.H004 {lam : ℤ} {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] (D : LatticeInput lam M) : Prop := by\\n  letI := D.vAdd\\n  letI := D.vMod\\n  exact (∀ w, D.h (D.x w) - D.x (D.h w) = (2:ℂ) • D.x w) ∧ (∀ w, D.h (D.y w) - D.y (D.h w) = (-2:ℂ) • D.y w) ∧ (∀ w, D.x (D.y w) - D.y (D.x w) = D.h w) ∧ D.v ≠ 0 ∧ D.x D.v = 0 ∧ D.h D.v = (lam:ℂ) • D.v ∧ (∀ i, D.basisV i = D.embed (D.basisM i)) ∧ Function.Injective D.embed ∧ LieIrreducible ℂ D.V D.x D.y D.h ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.xM m) = D.x (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.yM m) = D.y (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.hM m) = D.h (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.x r (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.y r (D.embed m))\\nnoncomputable def tensorAction {K : Type*} [Field K] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] [Module K (M ⊗[ℤ] K)] (f : M →ₗ[ℤ] M) : M ⊗[ℤ] K →ₗ[K] M ⊗[ℤ] K := TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K f\\n\"},\"parameters\":[{\"name\":\"K\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instK\",\"type\":\"Field K\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"p\",\"type\":\"ℕ\"},{\"name\":\"instChar\",\"type\":\"CharP K p\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"hp\",\"type\":\"Nat.Prime p\"},{\"name\":\"lam\",\"type\":\"ℤ\"},{\"name\":\"hLam\",\"type\":\"(0:ℤ) ≤ lam ∧ lam < (p:ℤ)\"},{\"name\":\"M\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instM\",\"type\":\"AddCommGroup M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"instModM\",\"type\":\"Module ℤ M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"instTensorK\",\"type\":\"Module K (M ⊗[ℤ] K)\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"D\",\"type\":\"LatticeInput lam M\"},{\"name\":\"hD\",\"type\":\"LatticeInput.H004 D\"}],\"premise_types\":{\"H001\":\"Nat.Prime p\",\"H002\":\"CharP K p\",\"H003\":\"(0:ℤ) ≤ lam ∧ lam < (p:ℤ)\",\"H004\":\"LatticeInput.H004 D\"},\"conclusion_type\":\"LieIrreducible K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) (tensorAction D.xM) (tensorAction D.yM) (tensorAction D.hM)\",\"representation\":\"The carrier V is a complex vector space of dimension lambda+1; M is an arbitrary free abelian lattice with a Z-basis whose image under an injective embedding is a C-basis of V. The operators x,y,h satisfy the stated sl2 relations and highest-weight conditions and restrict to integral operators on M; every divided power preserves M. Characteristic-zero irreducibility is included because accepted H004 explicitly states it. The target carrier is precisely M tensor_Z K in the source order, with K action and induced operators. The Module K typeclass binder supplies the scalar-extension module structure needed by this Lean tensor presentation; it is representation data, not an irreducibility assumption. p=2 and lambda=0 are retained; no distinctness of reduced h-weights is assumed. This representation and its fields require separate source-fidelity review.\",\"objects\":[],\"steps\":[{\"id\":\"T001\",\"statement\":\"LieIrreducible K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) (tensorAction D.xM) (tensorAction D.yM) (tensorAction D.hM)\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S001\",\"S002\",\"S003\",\"S004\",\"S005\",\"S006\",\"S007\",\"S008\"],\"explanation\":\"A single closed substantive implementation port for the accepted proof route, with the exact source-order conclusion. Its proof must establish the divided-power characteristic-zero basis and endpoint/action formulas; derive and calculate matrix units, including the composite with generally nonzero intermediate Y terms and unit binomial coefficients in Z_(p); analyze coordinate modules of the arbitrary localized lattice, compute fraction-field dimension before the rank-one generator and valuation argument; reduce the lattice basis and x,y,h matrices to M tensor_Z K; then use reduced matrix units on an arbitrary nonzero invariant subspace, choose a nonzero coordinate, and discharge the zero/nonzero cases. All witnesses remain local to the nonzero branch. This is an unproved theorem obligation for later workers, not a placeholder or an assumed field in the representation.\"}],\"terminal\":\"T001\",\"source_outputs\":{\"P\":\"T001\"}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferr